                                "sense_id": "958ae225-782b-3280-9ced-ec497dad675b",
                                "text": "There are approximately 1500 acres of potential candystick habitat in the Conservation Unit, which is located entirely within the analysis area, mainly in VRU 6."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b174e96-91d6-40cc-80eb-c49aacb027a4",
                                "sense_id": "958ae225-782b-3280-9ced-ec497dad675b",
                                "text": "This family also includes some unusual fleshy, chlorophyll-lacking plants, such as Indian pipe (Monotropa uniflora) and candystick (Allotropa virgata), which are saprophytic (feeding or growing upon dead or decaying organic matter)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6c8bc7d-ebd6-43e4-8c62-0e01ab8b28fd",
                                "sense_id": "958ae225-782b-3280-9ced-ec497dad675b",
                                "text": "Examples of them, shown in figure 7.1, are candystick (Allotropa virgata), pinesap (Monotropa hypopithys), Indian-pipe (Monotropa uniflora), and gnome-plant (Hemitomes congestum)."
                            }
